; Stage 14 LW-4 negative fixture: literal representability check.
;
; `300` does not fit `ui8` (max 255). Before LW-4 this silently truncated
; (`trunc i32 300 to i8` = 44, wrong code with no diagnostic); LW-4 tags every
; literal-sourced Val (`is-lit`/`lit-i64`, src/compiler-types.nuc) and checks
; it against the target width at the single int->int chokepoint in
; `coerce-int-val` (src/abi.nuc), here reached through the tier-2 widening
; adaptation at the call site. Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "integer literal 300 does not fit ui8"

(defn take8 (x:ui8):i32 (return (cast i32 x)))

(defn main ():i32
  (return (take8 300)))
